      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1874, when Douglas County’s border shifted, founders laid out six streets—Elbert, Jerry, Wilcox, Perry, Castle, and Front—to create Castle Rock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Rock%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s historic courthouse, built in 1889‑90, was destroyed by arson in 1978.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Rock%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Castle Rock Historical Museum now occupies the old Denver & Rio Grande depot on Elbert Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
